    "content": {
      "component": "blog_article",
      "title": "Celebrating 25 years of a gift that changed the lives of nursing and midwifery students",
      "description": "The Rufayda Al-Aslamiya stands tall today as a home away from home, and a centre of knowledge generation - transforming the lives of hundreds of students.",
      "date": "Jun 02, 2022",
      "read_time": "2 min read",
      "author": "Dr Rozina Karmaliani",
      "isGlobal": true,
      "banner_image": {
        "fieldtype": "asset",
        "_local": "19-Banner.jpg"
      },
      "thumbnail": {
        "fieldtype": "asset"
      },
      "languages": [],
      "show_share": true,
      "show_similar": true,
      "similar_show_header": true,
      "category": "",
      "isFeatured": null,
      "body": [
        {
          "component": "rich_text",
          "content": {
            "type": "doc",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "In the photo: The under-construction Rufayda Al-Aslamiya building then and now.",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "italic"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "It is often said, 'Education is the most powerful weapon you can use to change the world'. When brothers Alauddin and the late Badruddin Feerasta decided to support nursing education, little did they know of the impact that this contribution would have in bringing about a paradigm shift in higher education in nursing, and in the lives of countless individuals from all areas of Pakistan."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "In the 1990s, when the School of Nursing and Midwifery in Karachi, the Aga Khan University's first academic unit, needed an expansion to accommodate its growing academic needs, the Feerasta family came forward to support the construction of a new building that was designed to host classrooms, computer and science laboratories, a multimedia room, an audio-visual studio for blended learning, an auditorium with a seating capacity for hundreds, and the Dean's office. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Despite being the sole donors to the expansion project, when it came to naming the building, the family insisted on a name which demonstrated the impact of the nursing and midwifery professions. After thorough research, it was decided to name the building after Rufayda Al-Aslamiya, the first Muslim nurse, surgeon and social worker. "
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The Rufayda Al-Aslamaya building was inaugurated by the University's Chancellor, His Highness the Aga Khan, in 1996. The building has since hosted 25 batches of students and transformed the lives of hundreds of students. These graduates now serve as healthcare professionals throughout the world."
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "image",
                "attrs": {
                  "src": "/blogs/PublishingImages/Rufayda-building-group-photo.jpg",
                  "alt": ""
                }
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Feerasta family members along with AKU leadership at the Silver Jubilee anniversary of the Rufayda Al-Aslamiya building.",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "italic"
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Recently, the University hosted a ceremony to mark the Silver Jubilee anniversary of the building, which was attended by Alauddin, Nooruddin and Amin Feerasta, as well as other members of the Feerasta family and the AKU community. On the occasion, the family was delighted to hear from various nursing and other leaders about the impact of their contribution. AKU President Dr Sulaiman Shahabuddin thanked the family for their very generous gift and expressed his gratitude for their exemplary support to AKU over the years."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The short but beautifully planned ceremony served as a gentle reminder, motivation and celebration of philanthropy, academia and visionary leadership coming together to create an impact that is truly larger than life. The Rufayda Al-Aslamiya stands tall today as a home away from home, and a centre of knowledge generation - transforming the lives of hundreds of students who walk its corridors from across the country, and beyond."
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "hard_break"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
